<TeXmacs|2.1.4>

<style|<tuple|tmdoc|english>>

<\body>
  <tmdoc-title|Working on <TeXmacs>>

  These chapters are meant for developers who start working on the source
  code. The first one gives a map of the program: the directories of the
  source tree, the runtime data, the internal representation of documents
  and the way modifications flow through the program. The second one
  explains how to build <TeXmacs> with <name|CMake> or the autotools, how
  the packages for the various platforms are made, and how to run the
  automatic tests. The last one describes the documentation system itself:
  the style of the documentation, the help browser, the expansion of the
  documentation into books, and the rules for writing and validating
  developer documentation such as this guide.

  <\traverse>
    <branch|General architecture of <TeXmacs>|architecture.en.tm>

    <branch|Building <TeXmacs> and running the tests|build.en.tm>

    <branch|The documentation system|docsys.en.tm>
  </traverse>

